# ALLA HORNPIPE - Handel, Water Music, Suite No. 2 in D (HWV 349), no. 12.
# The format is in Demo1/CLAUDE.md, under "Song files". Instruments are tables with
# one entry per frame; each channel holds named tracks; the lines at the end are the
# order list. In a track '.' holds and '-' releases. '#' starts a comment.
#
# Written in 1717 for a concert on the Thames; Handel died in 1759, so it is public
# domain. The notes were read bar by bar off the full score in the Hallische
# Handel-Ausgabe (IMSLP 559922): the first section, bars 1 to 39, which Handel marks to
# be repeated - so the song loops it, as he did. The minor-key middle section and the
# da capo are not included. Nothing of the edition is copied but Handel's notes.
#
# What four channels keep of an orchestra. The movement is a conversation: strings state
# the tune, trumpets take it up, horns answer the trumpets, and everyone joins for the
# end of each phrase. Channels 1 and 2 play the two upper parts of whichever group has
# the tune - first and second violin, first and second trumpet, first and second horn -
# and change instrument when the tune changes hands. Channels 3 and 4 are one 16-bit
# bass, which is why the song can stay in Handel's D: the bass table would play D
# major's G and B 19 and 26 cents out, and the joined pair plays every note within a
# cent. The oboes, violas and third violins, who mostly double, are left out.
#
# Three things changed to fit:
# - The horns sound an octave below the trumpets, as the horns of Handel's day did,
#   so the answer is lower and darker than the call.
# - Where one group's last note overlaps the next group's first, the new phrase wins.
#   That is why a line here is half a bar: the entries all land on the fourth quarter,
#   and a line boundary is where a channel can change instrument.
# - The trills are left out.

song   ALLA HORNPIPE
key    D MAJOR
rows   6
beat   2

# The strings: in gently rather than struck, and no vibrato - steady tone.
instrument STRINGS
  table      tone
  volume     9 10 10 10 9 9 9 9 8
  distortion tone
  release    2

# The trumpets: struck hard, a level louder than anything else, then a steady tone.
instrument TRUMPET
  table      tone
  volume     13 12 11 11 10 10 10 10 9
  distortion tone
  release    2

# The horns: they swell in over three frames and sit below the trumpets.
instrument HORN
  table      tone
  volume     6 8 9 10 10 9 9 9 8
  distortion tone
  release    3

# Cello and violone together, on the 16-bit table: the bass line an octave below where
# it is written, as the violone played it.
instrument VIOLONE
  table      wide
  volume     12 11 10 10 9 9 9 8
  distortion tone
  release    3

channel 1 notes UPPER
  note  The top part of whoever has the tune: first violins, first trumpet or first horn.
  note  Each line is half a bar - three quarter notes - so a track name is its bar and
  note  half, 12A being the first half of bar 12. A track that names the trumpet or the
  note  horn plays it, and the rest are the strings.
  voice STRINGS
  track 1A  A4 . . . D5 .
  track 1B  . . E5 . . .
  track 2A  F#5 . D5 . . .
  track 2B  E5 . F#5 . D5 .
  track 3A  E5 . A5 . . .
  track 3B  E5 . F#5 . E5 D5
  track 5A  E5 . A4 . . .
  track 5B  . . - . . .
  track 7B  A5 . A5 . A5 .
  track 8A  A5 . G5 F#5 G5 .
  track 8B  G5 . G5 . G5 .
  track 9A  G5 . . . . .
  track 9B  A5 . F#5 . E5 .
  track 10A F#5 . G5 . E5 .
  track 10B . . . . D5 .
  track 11A @TRUMPET A4 . . . D5 .
  track 11B @TRUMPET . . E5 . . .
  track 12A @TRUMPET F#5 . D5 . . .
  track 12B @TRUMPET E5 . F#5 . D5 .
  track 13A @TRUMPET E5 . A5 . . .
  track 13B @TRUMPET E5 . F#5 . E5 D5
  track 14B @TRUMPET E5 . E5 . A4 .
  track 15A @HORN A3 . . . D4 .
  track 15B @HORN . . E4 . . .
  track 16A @HORN F#4 . D4 . . .
  track 16B @HORN E4 . F#4 . D4 .
  track 17A @HORN E4 . A4 . . .
  track 17B @HORN E4 . F#4 . E4 D4
  track TUTTI @TRUMPET A5 . A5 . A5 .
  track 19A @TRUMPET A5 . G5 F#5 G5 .
  track 19B @TRUMPET G5 . G5 . G5 .
  track 20A @TRUMPET G5 . F#5 E5 F#5 .
  track ECHO @HORN A4 . A4 . A4 .
  track 21A @HORN A4 . G4 F#4 G4 .
  track 21B @HORN G4 . G4 . G4 .
  track 22A @HORN G4 . F#4 E4 F#4 .
  track 22B D6 . D6 . D6 .
  track 23A D6 . C#6 B5 C#6 .
  track 23B C#6 . C#6 . C#6 .
  track 24A C#6 . B5 A5 B5 D6
  track 24B C#6 D6 B5 D6 C#6 D6
  track 25A E5 . . . . .
  track 25B E5 . A5 . . .
  track 26A . . D6 . C#6 .
  track 26B . . B5 . A5 .
  track 27A A5 . . . . .
  track 28A @TRUMPET G5 . A5 G5 F#5 .
  track 28B @TRUMPET A5 . G5 . F#5 .
  track 29A @TRUMPET F#5 . E5 D5 E5 .
  track 30A @HORN G4 . A4 G4 F#4 .
  track 30B @HORN A4 . G4 . F#4 .
  track 31A @HORN F#4 . E4 D4 E4 .
  track 33A @TRUMPET G5 . . . . .
  track 33B @TRUMPET A5 . F#5 . E5 .
  track 34A @TRUMPET F#5 . G5 . E5 .
  track 34B @TRUMPET . . . . D5 .
  track 35A @TRUMPET D5 . . . - .
  track 39A @TRUMPET D5 . . . . .

channel 2 notes LOWER
  note  The second part: second violins, second trumpet or second horn - and in bars 22
  note  to 26, where the violins climb to the top of their range together, the oboes
  note  underneath them.
  voice STRINGS
  track 1A  F#4 . . . A4 .
  track 1B  . . C#5 . . .
  track 2A  D5 . A4 . . .
  track 2B  C#5 . D5 . A4 .
  track 3A  C#5 . E5 . . .
  track 3B  C#5 . D5 . A4 .
  track 5A  C#5 . . . - .
  track 5B  A5 . A5 . A5 .
  track 6A  A5 . G5 F#5 G5 .
  track 6B  G5 . G5 . G5 .
  track 7A  G5 . F#5 E5 F#5 .
  track 7B  F#5 . F#5 . F#5 .
  track 8A  F#5 . E5 D5 E5 .
  track 8B  E5 . E5 . D5 .
  track 9A  C#5 . . . . .
  track 9B  C#5 . D5 . . .
  track 10A . . D5 . D5 .
  track 10B . . C#5 . . .
  track 11A @TRUMPET D4 . . . F#4 .
  track 11B @TRUMPET . . A4 . . .
  track 12A @TRUMPET D5 . F#4 . . .
  track 12B @TRUMPET A4 . D5 . F#4 .
  track 13A @TRUMPET A4 . E5 . . .
  track 13B @TRUMPET A4 . D5 . F#4 .
  track 14B @TRUMPET A4 . A4 . . .
  track 15A @HORN D3 . . . F#3 .
  track 15B @HORN . . A3 . . .
  track 16A @HORN D4 . F#3 . . .
  track 16B @HORN A3 . D4 . F#3 .
  track 17A @HORN A3 . E4 . . .
  track 17B @HORN A3 . D4 . F#3 .
  track 18B @HORN A3 . A3 . . .
  track 19A @TRUMPET F#5 . E5 D5 E5 .
  track 19B @TRUMPET E5 . E5 . E5 .
  track 20A @TRUMPET E5 . A4 . D5 .
  track ECHO @HORN F#4 . F#4 . F#4 .
  track 21A @HORN F#4 . E4 D4 E4 .
  track 21B @HORN E4 . E4 . E4 .
  track 22A @HORN E4 . A3 . D4 .
  track 22B F#5 . F#5 . F#5 .
  track 23A G#5 . . . - .
  track 23B E5 . A5 . E5 .
  track 24A F#5 . . . - .
  track 25A B4 . . . . .
  track 25B B4 . E5 . . .
  track 26A A5 . . . A5 .
  track 26B . . G#5 . . .
  track 27A C#4 . . . . .
  track TUTTI @TRUMPET F#5 . F#5 . F#5 .
  track 28A @TRUMPET E5 . F#5 E5 D5 .
  track 28B @TRUMPET F#5 . E5 . D5 .
  track 29A @TRUMPET D5 . F#4 . A4 .
  track 30A @HORN E4 . F#4 E4 D4 .
  track 30B @HORN F#4 . E4 . D4 .
  track 31A @HORN D4 . F#3 . A3 .
  track 33A @TRUMPET E5 . A4 . A4 .
  track 33B @TRUMPET A4 . D5 . A4 .
  track 34A @TRUMPET D4 . D4 . A4 .
  track 34B @TRUMPET A4 . A4 . A4 .
  track 35A @TRUMPET F#4 . . . - .
  track 39A @TRUMPET D4 . . . . .

channel 3 pair LOW BYTE
  note  The low byte of the bass. AUDCTL 28 joins channels 3 and 4 into one 16-bit
  note  counter on the 1.79 MHz clock, and this channel's own volume is never heard.

channel 4 notes BASS
  note  Cello and violone: the bass line an octave below where it is written, on the
  note  16-bit table, so every note is within a cent. It rests when the trumpets or the
  note  horns play alone - that silence is Handel's, and it is what makes the brass ring.
  voice VIOLONE
  track 1A  D2 . . . F#2 .
  track 1B  . . A2 . . .
  track 2A  D3 . F#2 . . .
  track 2B  A2 . D3 . F#2 .
  track 3A  A2 . C#3 . . .
  track 3B  A2 . D3 . F#2 .
  track 5A  A2 . . . - .
  track 5B  A2 . F#2 . A2 .
  track 6A  B2 . . . - .
  track 6B  G2 . E2 . G2 .
  track 7A  A2 . . . - .
  track 7B  F#2 . D2 . F#2 .
  track 8A  G2 . . . - .
  track 8B  E2 . G2 . E2 .
  track 9A  A2 . . . . .
  track 9B  A2 . D3 . . .
  track 10A . . G2 . A2 .
  track 10B . . A1 . . .
  track 11A D2 . . . . .
  track OFF - . . . . .
  track 20A A2 . . . D2 .
  track 20B . . - . . .
  track 22B D2 . B1 . D2 .
  track 23A E2 . . . - .
  track 23B C#2 . A1 . C#2 .
  track 24A D2 . . . - .
  track 24B B1 . D3 . D3 .
  track 25A D3 . . . . .
  track 25B D3 . C#3 . B2 .
  track 26A C#3 . A2 . E3 .
  track 26B . . E2 . . .
  track 27A A1 . . . . .
  track 27B . . - . . .
  track 31B F#2 . A2 . F#2 .
  track 32B E2 . G2 . E2 .
  track 33B A2 . B2 . . .
  track 35A D2 . D3 . A2 .
  track 35B F#2 . A2 . F#2 .
  track 36A B2 . . . . .
  track 38A G2 . . . A2 .

# The order list: a line is half a bar, so two lines make one bar of 3/2.
# Upper, lower, low byte, bass. The section loops, as Handel's repeat sign asks.
speed  13
audctl $28
loop
section STRINGS
line   1A    1A    .    1A
line   1B    1B    .    1B
line   2A    2A    .    2A
line   2B    2B    .    2B
line   3A    3A    .    3A
line   3B    3B    .    3B
line   3A    3A    .    3A
line   3B    3B    .    3B
line   5A    5A    .    5A
line   5B    5B    .    5B
line   .     6A    .    6A
line   .     6B    .    6B
line   .     7A    .    7A
line   7B    7B    .    7B
line   8A    8A    .    8A
line   8B    8B    .    8B
line   9A    9A    .    9A
line   9B    9B    .    9B
line   10A   10A   .    10A
line   10B   10B   .    10B
section TRUMPETS
line   11A   11A   .    11A
line   11B   11B   .    .
line   12A   12A   .    OFF
line   12B   12B   .    .
line   13A   13A   .    .
line   13B   13B   .    .
line   13A   13A   .    .
line   14B   14B   .    .
section HORNS
line   15A   15A   .    .
line   15B   15B   .    .
line   16A   16A   .    .
line   16B   16B   .    .
line   17A   17A   .    .
line   17B   17B   .    .
line   17A   17A   .    .
section TUTTI
line   TUTTI 18B   .    5B
line   19A   19A   .    6A
line   19B   19B   .    6B
line   20A   20A   .    20A
section HORNS
line   ECHO  ECHO  .    20B
line   21A   21A   .    .
line   21B   21B   .    .
line   22A   22A   .    .
section VIOLINS
line   22B   22B   .    22B
line   23A   23A   .    23A
line   23B   23B   .    23B
line   24A   24A   .    24A
line   24B   22B   .    24B
line   25A   25A   .    25A
line   25B   25B   .    25B
line   26A   26A   .    26A
line   26B   26B   .    26B
line   27A   27A   .    27A
section TRUMPETS
line   TUTTI TUTTI .    27B
line   28A   28A   .    .
line   28B   28B   .    .
line   29A   29A   .    .
section HORNS
line   ECHO  ECHO  .    .
line   30A   30A   .    .
line   30B   30B   .    .
line   31A   31A   .    .
section TUTTI
line   TUTTI TUTTI .    31B
line   19A   19A   .    6A
line   19B   19B   .    32B
line   33A   33A   .    9A
line   33B   33B   .    33B
line   34A   34A   .    10A
line   34B   34B   .    10B
line   35A   35A   .    35A
line   TUTTI TUTTI .    35B
line   19A   19A   .    36A
line   19B   19B   .    32B
line   33A   33A   .    9A
line   33B   33B   .    33B
line   34A   34A   .    38A
line   34B   34B   .    10B
line   39A   39A   .    11A
line   .     .     .    .
